WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.907
A function can return more than one result.

00:00:02.907 --> 00:00:09.817
Summarize receives a list of values, finds the minimum and maximum, and returns both.

00:00:09.817 --> 00:00:14.707
Python then unpacks those two results into low and high.

00:00:14.707 --> 00:00:19.646
With the current values, low is nine and high is twenty-one.

00:00:20.488 --> 00:00:26.372
This pattern is useful when one analytical function naturally produces several related metrics.
